[OPT_PARSER]
\par \--parser=STRING
Force parsing of the metadata file (if any) by the parser with the specified id.
Specifying an unavailable parser or a parser unable to read the input file will
result in an error.
\n\n
The following parsers are available if compiled into libarcsdec:
\htmlonly
<table class="m-table">
	<tr> <th>ID</th>                   <th>Description</th> </tr>
	<tr> <td><tt>cdrtoc</tt></td>      <td>Internal cdrdao/toc parser, experimental</td> </tr>
	<tr> <td><tt>cuesheet</tt></td>    <td>Internal CueSheet parser, experimental</td>   </tr>
	<tr> <td><tt>libcue</tt></td>      <td>Cuesheet parser based on libcue</td>          </tr>
</table>
\endhtmlonly
\manonly
.sp
.TS
tab(|);
ll.
ID       | Description
-------- | -----------
cdrtoc   | Internal cdrdao/toc parser, experimental
cuesheet | Internal Cuesheet parser, experimental
libcue   | Cuesheet parser based on libcue
.TE
.sp
\endmanonly
[OPT_PARSER]

